<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĭrĭdĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		viridis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>green color</i>, <i>greenness</i>,
				<i>verdure</i>, <i>viridity.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">herbescens viriditas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sen. 15, 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pratorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 16, 57</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 5, 20, § 76</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>freshness</i>, <i>briskness</i>, <i>vigor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senectus aufert eam viriditatem, in
					quā etiam nunc erat Scipio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 3, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vigere et habere quandam viriditatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 3, 31, 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurea illa amittit longo intervallo
					viriditatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Prov. Cons. 12, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
